  Layered on SRMDSICCore.xsd (org.mic-core.sic-core Classification): does not restate SIC Core's own unconditional Mandatory/Recommended/whitelist checks, only the attribute groups this level promotes from Recommended to Mandatory (6 at CL2). SIC Core's conformance clause forbids demoting its Mandatory attributes, so every level keeps the baseline.
  Never promoted at any level (12): design.model.quality-requirements, design.parameter.quality-requirements, design.test-case.quality-requirements, design.simulation-environment.quality-requirements, design.simulation-integration.quality-requirements, design.quality-assurance, design.verification, implementation.quality-assurance-results, implementation.verdict, evaluation.quality-assurance, evaluation.verdict, fulfillment.quality — the process record's own LifeCycleInformation/Signature is authoritative for sign-off; restating it here would create two mechanisms for one fact.
